 for bestpractices and # Settings / Preferences

## Overview
Design and implement a comprehensive Settings / Preferences subsystem for a multi-tenant enterprise OS. This prompts aims to deliver tenant- and user-level configuration capabilities across company profile, users & roles, integrations, AI & security settings, branding, and data retention. It also wires in related features: User Profile Management, Notifications & Alerts, and Integrations & Connectors, plus a robust Role & Permission model. All code must be runtime-safe with strict guards for null/undefined values before array operations, proper use of data ?? [] for Supabase-like results, Array.isArray() checks, and useState defaults for arrays. The deliverable should be production-ready, language- and framework-agnostic in structure but detailed enough to implement in a typical React + Node/Express or Next.js + Postgres/Supabase stack with a modular, scalable architecture.

CRITICAL: Dependency-first implementation order. Auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics tasks when both are present.

---

## Page Description (Full Detail)
What this page is:
- The Settings / Preferences page synthesizes tenant and user-level configuration into a single, scalable settings hub. It centralizes company profile data, user management (including roles and granular permissions), integrations management, AI-related security controls, branding choices, and data retention policies. It also serves as the governance layer for audit trails, feature flags, and auditability of settings changes.

Goals:
- Provide a secure, auditable, and scalable configuration surface for tenants and individual users with appropriate RBAC enforcement.
- Deliver connected experiences with:
  - User Profile Management: manage personal profile, preferences, authentication methods, and scoped API keys for builders.
  - Notifications & Alerts: in-app notifications, alert rules, scheduled report alerts, and integration with push/email delivery.
  - Integrations & Connectors: a connector framework to onboard OAuth/API key integrations, schedule/manual syncs, mapping, and error handling.
- Support branding and data retention policies at tenant scope, with per-user overrides where appropriate.
- Present a clean, modern UI per the design system, with a left-hand sidebar navigation (Company profile, Users, Roles & Permissions, Integrations, AI settings, Branding, Data policies, Audit trail, Feature flags) and contextual forms with inline validation, audit history, and change-tracking.

Features connected:
- User Profile Management
- Notifications & Alerts
- Integrations & Connectors
- Role & Permission (Tenant-level)
- Branding & Data Retention
- Audit Trail of settings changes
- Feature Flags (for staged rollouts)

UI elements and guidance:
- Settings sidebar with sections: Company, Users, Roles & Permissions, Integrations, AI settings, Branding, Data policies, Audit trail, Feature flags.
- Forms with inline validation and contextual help
- Audit trail view for settings changes
- Feature flag toggles for staged rollout visibility
- Consistent with the Visual Style, Typography, and Color Palette provided below
- Data visualizations and status indicators for integrations and live statuses where applicable

Visual guidance:
- Follow the provided design system and color palette; ensure high contrast, clear typographic hierarchy, and consistent UI density across all sub-pages.
- Emphasize security and governance with crisp separators, subdued borders, and accent indicators for alerts and live statuses.

Connected Features (detailed mappings):
- User Profile Management: personal profile, preferences, authentication methods, and scoped API keys for builders
- Notifications & Alerts: in-app notifications, alert rules, scheduled alerts, push/email integration
- Integrations & Connectors: OAuth/API key connectors, per-tenant configuration, sync scheduling, mapping, error handling
- Role & Permission: tenant-level roles with granular permissions
- Branding & Data Retention: logo/brand palette choices, data retention windows, data governance notes
- Audit Trail: tracking of settings changes for compliance
- Feature Flags: per-tenant or per-environment feature toggles for staged features

Connected Data Schemas (Role & Permission example):
- Role & Permission: Roles and granular permissions definitions for tenant-level access control
  - Fields example:
    - { "name": "id", "type": "uuid", "required": true, "description": "Role identifier" }
    - { "name": "companyId", "type": "uuid", "required": true, "description": "Tenant id" }
    - { "name": "name", "type": "string", "required": true, "description": "Role name" }
    - { "name": "permissions", "type": "array<string>", "required": true, "description": "List of permission keys" }
  - Relationships: { "type": "belongs_to", "description": "Role scoped to tenant", "targetTitle": "Company" }

API integration note:
- No external APIs are assumed to be connected directly in this task unless necessary to illustrate integration flows. The prompt should support internal API boundaries and clearly defined REST/GraphQL endpoints for CRUD operations on settings.

---

## Components to Build
- SettingsLayout: App shell with left navigation and content area; handles routing between sections.
- CompanyProfileForm: Tenant/company-wide settings (name, address, contact, branding defaults, logo, data retention policy, audit settings).
- UsersManagementPanel: List of users for the tenant, with create/edit/delete, status, and RBAC-aware actions.
- RolesPermissionsEditor: CRUD for Role records; assign granular permissions to roles; enforce tenant scoping.
- IntegrationsManager: Onboard OAuth/API key integrations, per-tenant configuration, status indicators, schedule sync settings, mapping definitions, and error handling UI.
- AIAndSecuritySettings: AI-related controls (safety, model access, role-aware prompts, data handling), security controls (2FA, authentication methods, scoped API keys for builders).
- BrandingSettingsPanel: Theme/brand colors, logo, typography presets, and per-tenant branding overrides (where allowed).
- DataPoliciesPanel: Data retention windows, export capabilities, deletion policies, audit configuration.
- NotificationsCenterSettings: In-app notification rules, alert rules, scheduled report alerts, and integration with push/email delivery services.
- AuditTrailView: Timeline/logs of settings changes with filters and export options.
- FeatureFlagsPanel: Toggle features per tenant, staging flags, and rollout visibility control.
- API Gateways/Adapters: Back-end integration points for connectors, OAuth flows, and sync tasks.
- ScopedApiKeyManager: For builders within User Profile Management, manage per-builder API keys with scoping and expiry.

Implementation notes:
- Ensure all components guard against null/undefined before using array methods (e.g., (items ?? []).map(...)).
- Use data ?? [] patterns for data sources that resemble Supabase results.
- Initialize useState with arrays for list-type data: useState<Type[]>([]).
- Validate API responses: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : [].
- Use optional chaining for nested API responses: obj?.prop?.subprop.

---

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend
- Tech stack alignment: React (or Next.js) with a component-based approach; TypeScript preferred for type safety.
- Routing: Settings as a top-level route with sub-pages: /settings/company, /settings/users, /settings/roles, /settings/integrations, /settings/ai, /settings/branding, /settings/data-policies, /settings/audit, /settings/flags.
- State management: Local component state with useState for small pieces; a shared context or minimal global store for tenant context, user session, and permissions.
- Forms: Inline validation, debounced validation where appropriate, and real-time hints.
- Accessibility: ARIA attributes, keyboard navigability, and proper focus management.
- UI/UX: Implement the Visual Style and UI Guidelines provided, including responsive behavior for 12-column grid and hero layout patterns.
- Data fetching: Abstract API layer with safe guards. All data reads must handle possible nulls using data ?? [] and Array.isArray checks.
- Audit trail: Client-side rendering of change events with timestamp, user, and delta; provide export options (CSV/JSON).

### Backend
- Data models (tables/entities) for:
  - Company (tenant)
  - User (belongs_to Company)
  - Role (belongs_to Company)
  - Permission (strings or enumerated keys)
  - UserRole/RoleAssignment (join table)
  - Integration (per-tenant)
  - BrandingSettings (per-tenant)
  - DataPolicy (per-tenant)
  - AuditLog (settings changes)
  - FeatureFlag (per-tenant)
  - BuilderApiKey (scoped API keys for builders)
  - AuditTrailEntry (detailed change records)
- Endpoints (examples; adapt to framework):
  - GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/companies
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
  - POST /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
  - GET /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
- Validation: Input validation on server-side; enforce authorization by tenant and role.
- Security: JWT/OAuth-based access; RBAC enforcement server-side; input sanitization; audit logging.

### Integration
- Component wiring:
  - SettingsLayout provides a persistent shell; each sub-page fetches tenant-scoped data and updates a shared tenant context.
  - Role-based access controls gate UI visibility and actions.
  - IntegrationsManager interacts with OAuth flows, stores tokens securely, and logs sync attempts and results.
  - Builder API keys are created with per-builder scoping and expiry; restricted to allowed actions by roles.
- Data flow:
  - All read/write go through a centralized API layer with guards for nulls; responses validated to arrays before mapping.
  - Supabase-like responses are normalized: data ?? [].
- Validation and error handling:
  - Client-side validation with inline feedback.
  - Server responses validated; client gracefully handles empty arrays or null payloads.

---

## User Experience Flow
- Admin signs in and navigates to Settings.
- Admin reviews Company Profile; edits branding defaults; saves changes; system logs an audit entry.
- Admin navigates to Users; creates a new user; assigns a Role; generates an initial password or invites user; audit trail updated.
- Admin configures Roles & Permissions; defines granular permissions; assigns to users/teams; validation ensures tenant isolation.
- Admin configures Integrations; onboards OAuth or API key connectors; tests connections; schedules/delays sync; mapping rules defined; logs stored.
- Admin adjusts AI & Security settings: manage allowed AI actions, model access, data handling settings; configure authentication methods per user/team.
- Admin updates Branding and Data Policies: update logos, color palettes, retention windows; save with audit.
- Admin configures Notifications Center: define alert rules, scheduled reports, and push/email delivery integrations.
- Admin toggles Feature Flags for staged rollouts; monitors effect via audit logs and usage metrics.
- All changes propagate to the audit trail, and possible live indicators (e.g., integration status or builder API key validity) appear in the UI.

---

## Build Order & Dependencies (Mandatory)
- Prerequisites:
  - Authentication and authorization system in place (RBAC with roles/permissions)
  - Tenant data model and basic User model exist
  - Core API scaffolding and database migrations for Company/Tenant
- Blocks:
  - If roles and permissions are incomplete, RolesPermissionsEditor cannot function
  - Integrations require OAuth/API key scaffolding and a Sync/Mapping layer
  - Audit trail requires logging infrastructure
- Sequencing Rule:
  - Auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both exist
  - Settings must be accessible to authorized admins; no tenant data leakage
  - Ensure runtime safety patterns (data ?? [], Array.isArray, useState([])) are enforced from the start

---

## Technical Specifications

### Data Models
- Company (Tenant)
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - name (string)
  - address (string)
  - contactEmail (string)
  - brandingSettingsId (FK -> BrandingSettings)
  - dataRetentionPolicyId (FK -> DataPolicy)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- User
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - email (string)
  - name (string)
  - isActive (boolean)
  - preferredAuthMethod (enum: password, mfa, oauth, etc.)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- Role
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - name (string)
  - permissions (string[]) — list of permission keys
  - description (string)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- Permission (enum or reference table)
  - key (string, PK)
  - description (string)

- UserRole (association)
  - userId (uuid)
  - roleId (uuid)

- Integration
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - type (string) // e.g., "HubSpot", "GoogleDrive"
  - config (jsonb)
  - status (enum: connected, disconnected, error, syncing)
  - lastSyncAt (timestamp)
  - nextSyncAt (timestamp)
  - mapping (jsonb)
  - errorLogs (array<string>)

- BrandingSettings
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - logoUrl (string)
  - primaryColor (string)
  - secondaryColor (string)
  - fontPreset (string)

- DataPolicy
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - retentionPeriodDays (integer)
  - exportAllowed (boolean)
  - purgeScheduled (boolean)

- AuditLog
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid)
  - userId (uuid)
  - action (string)
  - changes (jsonb)
  - createdAt

- FeatureFlag
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid)
  - featureName (string)
  - enabled (boolean)
  - rolloutPercentage (integer)

- BuilderApiKey
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - builderId (uuid)
  - key (string)
  - tenantId/companyId (uuid)
  - scopes (string[])
  - expiresAt (timestamp)
  - createdAt

- AuditTrailEntry
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - action (string)
  - actorUserId (uuid)
  - tenantId (uuid)
  - details (jsonb)
  - timestamp

### API Endpoints
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/company
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/company
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
- PUT /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users/{userId}
- DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users/{userId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles/{roleId}
- DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles/{roleId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations/{integrationId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
- POST /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
- GET /api/builders/{builderId}/keys

### Security
- RBAC enforcement at both UI and API layers
- JWT/OAuth tokens; scope-based access
- Credential storage security for API keys and OAuth tokens
- Audit logging for all settings changes and sensitive actions
- Input validation and server-side sanitization

### Validation
- All API responses must be validated and normalized:
  - const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - data ?? [] for list-like results
- Client-side guards for arrays:
  - (items ?? []).map(...)
- Optional chaining for nested API structures: obj?.prop?.sub
- Destructuring with defaults: const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}

---

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Admin can view and edit Company Profile, Branding, Data Policies, and Audit Trail entries with proper RBAC restrictions.
- [ ] Users: Create, edit, deactivate, and assign Roles with granular permissions. Role editor enforces tenant scoping.
- [ ] Roles & Permissions: Roles defined, permissions enforced in UI and API; changes are auditable.
- [ ] Integrations: Onboard OAuth/API-key connectors; test connections; schedule synchronization; error handling and mapping configured; status reflects live state.
- [ ] Notifications & Alerts: In-app notifications configured; alert rules and scheduled reports deliver via push/email; delivery status visible.
- [ ] User Profile Management: Users can manage own profile; scoped API keys created for builders with proper restrictions.
- [ ] Feature Flags: Per-tenant feature toggles with rollout configuration; changes appear in audit logs.
- [ ] Data retention and export capabilities function as defined; retention windows enforced.
- [ ] Accessibility and keyboard navigation are functional across all components.
- [ ] All API reads handle potential null/undefined values safely; all lists are guarded as per runtime safety rules.
- [ ] Visual design aligns with the provided color palette, typography, and layout guidelines.

---

## UI/UX Guidelines
Apply the project's design system to all components:
- Follow the Visual Style and Color Palette provided
- Use Poppins/Manrope for headings and Inter/Roboto for UI text
- Implement 12-column responsive grid with the hero-left, card-right composition for the Settings overview
- Cards: deep surfaces with subtle inner shadows and light borders
- Interactive elements: clear focus states and hover feedback
- Data visualizations: minimal, precise, and accessible
- Consistent micro-UI patterns for chips, pills, and tag outlines

---

## Visual Style

Color Palette (as provided)
- Background primary: #05060A
- Center glow: gradient #071228 → #0B1A2A
- Surface / cards: #0F1720
- Inset panels: #0C1116
- Primary accent: #9AD0FF
- Secondary accent: #154E78
- Live indicator: #00D27A
- Neutral text: #8FA0B0
- Strong text: #F7FAFF
- Subtle borders: rgba(255,255,255,0.03)
- Primary CTA: #FFFFFF
- Dark CTA text: #081017
- Secondary filled/toggle: #0F1720

Typography & Layout
- Headings: Poppins/Manrope, weights 700–900, desktop hero H1 56–96px
- Body: Inter/Roboto, 400–600
- Micro-labels: 10–12px uppercase
- 12-column grid with generous gutters; hero left 6–7 columns, right 4–5 columns
- Spacing: base 8px scale; paddings/margins 8/16/24/32/48/64

Key Design Elements
- Cards: rounded 12–16px, gradient/light stroke, hover elevation
- Navigation: top-centered links, top-right white pill CTA
- Data Visualization: pale blue lines, neon green accents
- Buttons/Inputs: primary pills, ghost/dark, micro-pills; focus rings in pale blue
- Live indicators: neon green pulse

Design Philosophy
- Modern, enterprise-grade, data-first clarity
- Minimal clutter; scalable components
- Secure, auditable, tenant-isolated experience

---

## Mandatory Coding Standards — Runtime Safety

CRITICAL: All generated code must guard against null/undefined before array methods.

1. Supabase-like data: use nullish coalescing when reading lists:
   - const items = data ?? []
2. Array methods safety:
   - (items ?? []).map(...)
   - Array.isArray(items) ? items.map(...) : []
3. React useState defaults for arrays:
   - useState<Type[]>([])
4. API response validation:
   - const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
5. Optional chaining:
   - obj?.property?.nested
6. Destructuring with defaults:
   - const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}

