- RolesPermissionsEditor: CRUD for Role records; assign granular permissions to roles; enforce tenant scoping.
- IntegrationsManager: Onboard OAuth/API key integrations, per-tenant configuration, status indicators, schedule sync settings, mapping definitions, and error handling UI.
- AIAndSecuritySettings: AI-related controls (safety, model access, role-aware prompts, data handling), security controls (2FA, authentication methods, scoped API keys for builders).
- BrandingSettingsPanel: Theme/brand colors, logo, typography presets, and per-tenant branding overrides (where allowed).
- DataPoliciesPanel: Data retention windows, export capabilities, deletion policies, audit configuration.
- NotificationsCenterSettings: In-app notification rules, alert rules, scheduled report alerts, and integration with push/email delivery services.
- AuditTrailView: Timeline/logs of settings changes with filters and export options.
- FeatureFlagsPanel: Toggle features per tenant, staging flags, and rollout visibility control.
- API Gateways/Adapters: Back-end integration points for connectors, OAuth flows, and sync tasks.
- ScopedApiKeyManager: For builders within User Profile Management, manage per-builder API keys with scoping and expiry.

Implementation notes:
- Ensure all components guard against null/undefined before using array methods (e.g., (items ?? []).map(...)).
- Use data ?? [] patterns for data sources that resemble Supabase results.
- Initialize useState with arrays for list-type data: useState<Type[]>([]).
- Validate API responses: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : [].
- Use optional chaining for nested API responses: obj?.prop?.subprop.

---

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend
- Tech stack alignment: React (or Next.js) with a component-based approach; TypeScript preferred for type safety.
- Routing: Settings as a top-level route with sub-pages: /settings/company, /settings/users, /settings/roles, /settings/integrations, /settings/ai, /settings/branding, /settings/data-policies, /settings/audit, /settings/flags.
- State management: Local component state with useState for small pieces; a shared context or minimal global store for tenant context, user session, and permissions.
- Forms: Inline validation, debounced validation where appropriate, and real-time hints.
- Accessibility: ARIA attributes, keyboard navigability, and proper focus management.
- UI/UX: Implement the Visual Style and UI Guidelines provided, including responsive behavior for 12-column grid and hero layout patterns.
- Data fetching: Abstract API layer with safe guards. All data reads must handle possible nulls using data ?? [] and Array.isArray checks.
- Audit trail: Client-side rendering of change events with timestamp, user, and delta; provide export options (CSV/JSON).

### Backend
- Data models (tables/entities) for:
  - Company (tenant)
  - User (belongs_to Company)
  - Role (belongs_to Company)
  - Permission (strings or enumerated keys)
  - UserRole/RoleAssignment (join table)
  - Integration (per-tenant)
  - BrandingSettings (per-tenant)
  - DataPolicy (per-tenant)
  - AuditLog (settings changes)
  - FeatureFlag (per-tenant)
  - BuilderApiKey (scoped API keys for builders)
  - AuditTrailEntry (detailed change records)
- Endpoints (examples; adapt to framework):
  - GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/companies
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
  - POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
  - GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
  - PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
  - POST /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
  - GET /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
- Validation: Input validation on server-side; enforce authorization by tenant and role.
- Security: JWT/OAuth-based access; RBAC enforcement server-side; input sanitization; audit logging.

### Integration
- Component wiring:
  - SettingsLayout provides a persistent shell; each sub-page fetches tenant-scoped data and updates a shared tenant context.
  - Role-based access controls gate UI visibility and actions.
  - IntegrationsManager interacts with OAuth flows, stores tokens securely, and logs sync attempts and results.
  - Builder API keys are created with per-builder scoping and expiry; restricted to allowed actions by roles.
- Data flow:
  - All read/write go through a centralized API layer with guards for nulls; responses validated to arrays before mapping.
  - Supabase-like responses are normalized: data ?? [].
- Validation and error handling:
  - Client-side validation with inline feedback.
  - Server responses validated; client gracefully handles empty arrays or null payloads.

---

## User Experience Flow
- Admin signs in and navigates to Settings.
- Admin reviews Company Profile; edits branding defaults; saves changes; system logs an audit entry.
- Admin navigates to Users; creates a new user; assigns a Role; generates an initial password or invites user; audit trail updated.
- Admin configures Roles & Permissions; defines granular permissions; assigns to users/teams; validation ensures tenant isolation.
- Admin configures Integrations; onboards OAuth or API key connectors; tests connections; schedules/delays sync; mapping rules defined; logs stored.
- Admin adjusts AI & Security settings: manage allowed AI actions, model access, data handling settings; configure authentication methods per user/team.
- Admin updates Branding and Data Policies: update logos, color palettes, retention windows; save with audit.
- Admin configures Notifications Center: define alert rules, scheduled reports, and push/email delivery integrations.
- Admin toggles Feature Flags for staged rollouts; monitors effect via audit logs and usage metrics.
- All changes propagate to the audit trail, and possible live indicators (e.g., integration status or builder API key validity) appear in the UI.

---

## Build Order & Dependencies (Mandatory)
- Prerequisites:
  - Authentication and authorization system in place (RBAC with roles/permissions)
  - Tenant data model and basic User model exist
  - Core API scaffolding and database migrations for Company/Tenant
- Blocks:
  - If roles and permissions are incomplete, RolesPermissionsEditor cannot function
  - Integrations require OAuth/API key scaffolding and a Sync/Mapping layer
  - Audit trail requires logging infrastructure
- Sequencing Rule:
  - Auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both exist
  - Settings must be accessible to authorized admins; no tenant data leakage
  - Ensure runtime safety patterns (data ?? [], Array.isArray, useState([])) are enforced from the start

