## Technical Specifications

### Data Models
- Company (Tenant)
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - name (string)
  - address (string)
  - contactEmail (string)
  - brandingSettingsId (FK -> BrandingSettings)
  - dataRetentionPolicyId (FK -> DataPolicy)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- User
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - email (string)
  - name (string)
  - isActive (boolean)
  - preferredAuthMethod (enum: password, mfa, oauth, etc.)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- Role
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - name (string)
  - permissions (string[]) — list of permission keys
  - description (string)
  - createdAt, updatedAt

- Permission (enum or reference table)
  - key (string, PK)
  - description (string)

- UserRole (association)
  - userId (uuid)
  - roleId (uuid)

- Integration
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - type (string) // e.g., "HubSpot", "GoogleDrive"
  - config (jsonb)
  - status (enum: connected, disconnected, error, syncing)
  - lastSyncAt (timestamp)
  - nextSyncAt (timestamp)
  - mapping (jsonb)
  - errorLogs (array<string>)

- BrandingSettings
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - logoUrl (string)
  - primaryColor (string)
  - secondaryColor (string)
  - fontPreset (string)

- DataPolicy
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid, FK)
  - retentionPeriodDays (integer)
  - exportAllowed (boolean)
  - purgeScheduled (boolean)

- AuditLog
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid)
  - userId (uuid)
  - action (string)
  - changes (jsonb)
  - createdAt

- FeatureFlag
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - companyId (uuid)
  - featureName (string)
  - enabled (boolean)
  - rolloutPercentage (integer)

- BuilderApiKey
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - builderId (uuid)
  - key (string)
  - tenantId/companyId (uuid)
  - scopes (string[])
  - expiresAt (timestamp)
  - createdAt

- AuditTrailEntry
  - id (uuid, PK)
  - action (string)
  - actorUserId (uuid)
  - tenantId (uuid)
  - details (jsonb)
  - timestamp

### API Endpoints
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/company
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/company
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users
- PUT /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users/{userId}
- DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/users/{userId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles/{roleId}
- DELETE /api/tenants/{tenantId}/roles/{roleId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/integrations/{integrationId}
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/branding
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/data-policies
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
- POST /api/tenants/{tenantId}/audit
- GET /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
- PATCH /api/tenants/{tenantId}/feature-flags
- POST /api/builders/{builderId}/keys
- GET /api/builders/{builderId}/keys

### Security
- RBAC enforcement at both UI and API layers
- JWT/OAuth tokens; scope-based access
- Credential storage security for API keys and OAuth tokens
- Audit logging for all settings changes and sensitive actions
- Input validation and server-side sanitization

### Validation
- All API responses must be validated and normalized:
  - const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - data ?? [] for list-like results
- Client-side guards for arrays:
  - (items ?? []).map(...)
- Optional chaining for nested API structures: obj?.prop?.sub
- Destructuring with defaults: const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}

